==Strategy==
Bring lots of Anti-Alien units, especially those with Freeze or Knockback abilities, in addition to your regular crew of heavy damage dealers like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut]] or other High DPS Ubers. If you don't have any anti-alien unit that knock backs or weakens, use ( at least ) 4 meatshield. This stage will prove difficult without at least one heavy hitting Uber to pair with Bahamut. If you don't have any good ranged units, this stage will be quite difficult but you can still try with the likes of [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Sexy Legs]] ( preferably TF ) and the obvious Gacha like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris]]/[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Hacker]] and some anti-aliens. Weaken is a huge boon here as it buys you lots of time to stall vs the big guys, and if you have [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Surfer]] or [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Psychocat]] you can slow down Cyberhorn's progress and make stalling much easier. [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Cat]] is also very helpful for knocking back the Cyberhorn and Imperator Sael.

At the start, you have very little time to stall but a few peons do get sent your way early. Baa Baa, Doge and a Squire Rel all do very little to advance your cash flow until Imperator Sael and Cyberhorn start to advance so only put one level into Worker Cat. Save for a heavy hitter to clear out peons and then get your Alien-freeze units out stat because Teacher Bear shows up about 60 seconds into the map to slowly make his way to your base. Try to get your Bahamut out before Teacher Bear comes, as Bahamut can hit Teacher Bear after the Imperator Sael and Cyberhorn are dead.

There is no boss wave, you will just have to work your way to stall them until the big threats stop respawning, if you don't rush the stage out. Thankfully, there are only 2 of each of the big enemies, so once you take down the 2nd wave of Bear, Horn and Sael, you win.

